    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0603" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1/122: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-02-08T14:00:00+00:00">February 8, 1936—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 8—10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Your 47, February 6, 2 p.m. According to reliable information the rumor,
                    which has likewise been current here, is believed to have originated in the
                    United States. A responsible and informed official of the Colonial Office when
                    questioned about it is reported to have made the reply that the United States
                    had not yet been officially consulted about the conference and that he had no
                    knowledge as to the source of the rumor.</p>
                <pb facs="0604" n="524" xml:id="pg524"/>
                <p>A meeting took place 2 days ago between British representatives and Javanese. The
                    British have not yet had time to reach any decision as a result of this
                    conference. Further information may be available early next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
